WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome to the show, fellas
-Yeah!

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah!
-Whoo!

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is lovely to have you back
in the building.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
We first met when
I was on "SNL,"

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you guys were writers fo
the previous iteration of

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.143 line:92%
"Late Night" with Jimmy Fallon

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.312
-That's right. That's right.
It's good to be back here.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were there for like
four years.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were, like,
literally, I think,

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:16.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
like the fourth or
fifth people they hired.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:17.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
-The building was empty.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:22.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The building was empty.
And you guys met in college?

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We met in college.
-Yeah.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
We were not studying.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
We decided to just, you know
spend all that time

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
trying to be funny
and make everybody

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:30.864 size:84% position:42% line:92%
in the lunchroom laugh.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:33.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah, we actually met
in an a cappella group,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
because that's where
the cool kids --

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.237 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure, sure. Yes.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, usually,
like, no nerds allowed.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, no.
-No, no.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:44.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nerds, please.
You got to get recruited.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. And this was at Harvard
so you have to have

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
a place where no nerds
are allowed.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.149 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right. Yeah, yeah.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:50.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Or, otherwise,
they'll just be everywhere

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They'll be everywhere, man.
-You were a deejay.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.321 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Graveyard shift.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Actually, okay,
embarrassing story.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:59.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
I fell asleep in
the law library one night.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.260 line:92%
And lost my term-time job.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.662
So I actually just started
you know, spinning records

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I would charge less than
the other deejays,

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:06.499 size:75% position:38% line:92%
so that was how I --

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And is it true that you wer
2:00 to 6:00 a.m.?

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Oh, yeah, on WHRB.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
We had a radio show.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:15.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, by the way,
if you are a radio deejay

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:17.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
at that time of night,
the only people calling in

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:19.212 size:81% position:41% line:92%
are usually prisoners.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Prisoners.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Shout-out,
Bill and Rick in prison.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:24.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, shout-out to
Bill and Rick in prison.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.220 line:92%
Eric in E-block, I see you, man.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.857 line:92%
Hey, my man, we made it, bro

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.492 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Two of us made it.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.327 size:84% position:42%
But I would bring him
to the studio sometimes

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:35.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I would be like,
"Hey, Bashir,

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
will you pretend to be, like
a dance-hall artist?"

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.432
And, so, I'd be like,
"Hey, in the studio with me now,

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:43.670
I have a Jamaican artist
Blue Nile Crocodile Ranks.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.472 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Go on, bred'ren.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:45.905 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.507
-And then, of course, our
Jamaican friends would say

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:48.308 line:92%
"We don't sound like that.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"That is the fakest patoi
I've ever heard."

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.644 line:92%
Please don't ever do that again.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys -- This is very hard
to accomplish,

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.181 line:92%
and I want to congratulate you

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have two shows
on the air right now.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
-Yeah, thank you. Yeah.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have
"Sherman's Showcase" on IFC.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.254 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you have "South Side"
on Comedy Central.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.557 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-"South Side," yeah.

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:07.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And "South Side" -- Bashir,
your wife is in the show,

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.962 line:92%
and your brother is in the show.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:12.565
-My business/writing partner
two of my boys from high school.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
Literally every child
my mother had

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:18.004 line:92%
is on that air at some point

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did it sort of --
Did the idea for the show

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:22.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
come from the fact that yo
had so many people

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
that fit into
this story so well?

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:26.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know what it wa
is that

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:28.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
we wanted to do a show
about one of our hometowns

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:30.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
Originally, we were going
to do a show about

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.584 line:92%
Diallo's hometown of Atlanta

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:32.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
ATL in the house.
-Yep.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.287
-But we ended up doing a show --
-Whoo!

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.989 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hey, the one guy.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
We ended up doing a show
about Chicago.

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:39.459
You know, so much about what you
hear about the city is --

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:41.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's maligned
and it's, like, tough stuff,

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm like, "That's not
what I grew up with.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.598 line:92%
My city is vibrant and fun."

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we thought,
"Let's have Chicagoans

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.101 size:81% position:41% line:92%
speak for themselves."

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
So most of the folks you see
on our show --

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:50.904 line:92%
not even professional actors

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:52.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
just the funniest people
we know.

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I should point out that
it is also --

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:57.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:59.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's also honest and authentic
-Yes.

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:01.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It doesn't run away from
the things that are

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.184
true about Chicago,
but it also shows that it is not

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.451 size:75% position:38% line:92%
this dire situation.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:05.852 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, no.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
We start from the reality,
but we say the people

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
who live there -- you know
they don't walk around all day

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
with their heads,
you know, hanging down,

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.193
trying to figure out how to make
it through another day

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:15.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
while blues plays in
the background.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:18.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which, by the way, would
be amazing.

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, no, they find joy
and they find spark

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:21.501 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and they find spirit.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, once the city
started showing

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:26.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
its true colors to America
the response has been amazing.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.307 line:92%
Season 2 is happening, y'all

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:30.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's going to be a great time.
[ Cheers and applause ]

